  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1022 PM MDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nAn upper high will center itself over the TX/OK panhandle Sunday \nafternoon, then shifts slightly eastward to the Red River area \nMonday. CAMs suggest much of the storm activity tomorrow to be over \nthe area mountains with more scattered activity in the lowlands. \nMoisture will still be well above average Sunday with modeled PWs \nupwards of around 1.4\". Monday through Wednesday storm chances look \nto focus over the area mountains and locations west of the Rio \nGrande. PWs continue to stay above average at around 1.1\"-1.3\" \ndepending on day and location, but either way - moderate to heavy \nrain will continue to be possible with thunderstorms which could \nlead to flooding. Not expecting any crazy flooding threat days at \nthis time.\n\nBy later in the week, high pressure rapidly dissolves to our east \nand redevelops over SoCal. Long range models seem uncertain as to if \nhigh pressure will stay in this general area or if the high will be \ndissolved by an upper trough swinging through to our north.",
